  "content": "[Intro]\n[G]  [Em7]\n[Am7]  [D]\n[G]  [Em7]\n[Am7][D]That's\n\n[Verse 1]\n[G]life, that's what all\n[B7]the people say\n[Em7]You're riding high in April\n[A7]Shot down in May But I\n[G]know I'm gonna [B7]change that\n[Em7]tune When I'm\n[A7]back on top, back on top in June\n[D7]I said, that's life,\n[G]and\n[B7]as funny as it may seem\n[Em7]Some people get their kicks\n[A7]Stompin' on a dream\n[G]But I don't let it, [B7]let it get me down\n[Em7]'Cause this\n[A7]fine old world [D7]it keeps spinnin'\n[G]around I've been a\n\n[Chorus]\n[G7]puppet, a pauper, a pirate A poet,\na pawn and a king I've been\n[C6]up and down and over and out\nAnd I know one thing Each\n[A7]time I find myself\nflat on my face I\n[D7]pick myself up and get\nback in the race That's\n\n[Verse 2]\n[G]life, I tell ya,\n[B7]I can't deny it\n[Em7]I thought of quitting, baby\n[A7]But my heart just ain't gonna buy it And\n[G]if I didn't think it was [B7]worth one single\n[Em7]try I'd jump\n[A7]right on a big bird [D7]and then I'd fly\n[G]I've been a\n\n[Chorus]\n[G7]puppet, a pauper, a pirate A poet,\na pawn and a king I've been\n[C6]up and down and over and out\nAnd I know one thing Each\n[A7]time I find myself layin'\nflat on my face I just\n[D7]pick myself up and get\n[Eb7]back in the race That's\n\n[Verse 3]\n[Ab]life, that's life\n[C7]And I can't deny it\n[Fm]Many times I thought of cuttin' out\n[Bb7]but my heart won't buy it But\n[Ab]if there's nothing [C7]shakin' come this here Ju-\n\n[Outro]\n[Fm]ly [Bb7]\nI'm gonna roll\n[Bb7]myself up in a\n[Eb7]big ball\nand\n[Ab]die [Cb]\n[E9]  [Eb7]\n[Amaj7(b5)]My,\n[Ab]my",
